th-to-node=3D"14">4. Why this survives without NTP</h3><ol start=3D"1" data=
-path-to-node=3D"15"><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"15,0,0"><b data-path-to-no=
de=3D"15,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">The Oracle:</b> The <code data-path-=
to-node=3D"15,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"16">UPDATE ... WHERE expiryTime &l=
t; CURRENT_TIMESTAMP</code> statement uses the Database's clock. If the DB =
thinks it's 10:00 AM, the lock expires at 10:00 AM, even if your App Server=
 thinks it's 9:55 AM.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"15,1,0"><b data-p=
ath-to-node=3D"15,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">The Token:</b> Because the =
<code data-path-to-node=3D"15,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"23">fencingToken</=
