48">long</code> (1, 2, 3...), it is clock-agnostic. It=E2=80=99s just a "Nu=
mber of the current lease."</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"15,2,0"><b =
data-path-to-node=3D"15,2,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">The TTL:</b> If the A=
pp Server is off by 5 seconds, it sends a <code data-path-to-node=3D"15,2,0=
" data-index-in-node=3D"59">Duration.ofMinutes(10)</code> to the DB. The DB=
 adds exactly 600 seconds to <b data-path-to-node=3D"15,2,0" data-index-in-=
node=3D"128">its own</b> current time. The relative time is perfectly prese=
rved.</p></li></ol><h3 data-path-to-node=3D"16">Final Production Layout Tip=
:</h3><ul data-path-to-node=3D"17"><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"17,0,0"><b d=
ata-path-to-node=3D"17,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">PostgreSQL/MySQL:</b> =
Ensure your <code data-path-to-node=3D"17,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"30">ex=
piryTime</code> column is a <code data-path-to-node=3D"17,0,0" data-index-i=
n-node=3D"53">TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE</code> (or equivalent) to avoid DST =
(Daylight Savings) issues.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"17,1,0"><b d=
ata-path-to-node=3D"17,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Index:</b> Ensure <cod=
e data-path-to-node=3D"17,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"14">resourceId</code> =
is the Primary Key to prevent the race condition on row creation.</p></li><=
/ul><p data-path-to-node=3D"18">This architecture is "NTP-Immune" for data =
integrity. The only cost is that your application logs might look a little =
